  "id": "norm",
  "term": "norm",
  "definition": "In social psychology, a norm is a shared expectation or common pattern of behavior that people use to guide decisions. People may follow norms to gain approval, avoid disapproval, simplify choices, and, in uncertain situations, reduce negative feelings.",
